1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,586
In 1932,

2
00:00:01,586 --> 00:00:03,815
Australia's army went to war...

3
00:00:03,815 --> 00:00:04,779
against BIRDS.

4
00:00:04,779 --> 00:00:06,070
With machine guns.

5
00:00:06,070 --> 00:00:08,067
Western Australia.

6
00:00:08,067 --> 00:00:10,563
Wheat farmers, many of them war veterans,

7
00:00:10,563 --> 00:00:12,234
were hit hard by the Depression.

8
00:00:12,234 --> 00:00:13,836
Then around 20,000 emus

9
00:00:13,836 --> 00:00:16,014
showed up... and ate their crops.

10
00:00:16,014 --> 00:00:18,394
So the government sent soldiers.

11
00:00:18,394 --> 00:00:20,565
2 Lewis machine guns.

12
00:00:20,565 --> 00:00:22,704
10,000 rounds.

13
00:00:22,704 --> 00:00:23,911
Day 3:

14
00:00:23,911 --> 00:00:26,907
over 1,000 emus walk up to a dam.

15
00:00:26,907 --> 00:00:28,129
Perfect ambush.

16
00:00:28,129 --> 00:00:29,441
The gun kills about a dozen...

17
00:00:29,441 --> 00:00:30,794
and JAMS.

18
00:00:30,794 --> 00:00:32,315
They mounted a gun on a truck.

19
00:00:32,315 --> 00:00:34,014
The emus outran the truck.

20
00:00:34,014 --> 00:00:35,535
By December, the Major reported

21
00:00:35,535 --> 00:00:39,738
986 kills with 9,860 rounds.

22
00:00:39,738 --> 00:00:42,450
EXACTLY 10 bullets per bird.

23
00:00:42,450 --> 00:00:43,959
And the emu problem?

24
00:00:43,959 --> 00:00:45,016
Still there.

25
00:00:45,016 --> 00:00:47,303
So what actually worked?

26
00:00:47,303 --> 00:00:49,669
Not soldiers. Money.

27
00:00:49,669 --> 00:00:51,573
The government kept paying farmers a cash

28
00:00:51,573 --> 00:00:53,640
bounty per emu.

29
00:00:53,640 --> 00:00:55,950
In 6 months of 1934,

30
00:00:55,950 --> 00:00:59,420
they filed over 57,000 bounty claims.

31
00:00:59,420 --> 00:01:01,881
Turns out the deadliest weapon in that war...

32
00:01:01,881 --> 00:01:02,961
wasn't a gun.

33
00:01:02,961 --> 00:01:05,200
It was a paycheck.
